# Package manager files
#
# package-lock.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It used to be, and that is
# what "builds locally, fails on Vercel" meant: without the lockfile Vercel
# re-resolved every caret range from scratch, so it built a dependency set
# nobody had ever type-checked. On 2026-09-09 that set was
# @supabase/supabase-js 2.116.0 against the 2.52.0 we develop on -- 64 minor
# versions of drift in the library that generates our database types -- plus
# TypeScript 5.9 against 5.8. `npx tsc --noEmit` passed locally with 0 errors
# and the same command over Vercel's resolution produced 122.
#
# That is also why next.config.js survived since July with
# ignoreBuildErrors: true. The errors it was suppressing were never in our
# code; they were in a dependency tree that only ever existed on Vercel.
#
# Ignoring a lockfile does not save a meaningful amount of upload; it only
# removes the guarantee that CI builds what you tested. Do not re-add it.
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml